Page 1: Properties ka quick revision
Property	       Easy English meaning
display: flex	   Creates a flex container.
flex-direction	   Sets the direction of items.
flex-wrap	       Allows items to move onto new lines.
flex-flow	       Shorthand for direction and wrapping.
justify-content	   Aligns items along the main axis.
align-items	       Aligns items along the cross axis.
align-content	   Arranges multiple flex lines.
gap	               Adds space between items.
order	           Changes the visual order of an item.
flex-grow	       Controls how an item grows.
flex-shrink	       Controls how an item shrinks.
flex-basis	       Sets an item's initial main size.
flex	           Shorthand for grow, shrink and basis.
align-self	       Aligns one item differently.


<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>CSS Flexbox Properties</title>

<style>
* { box-sizing: border-box; }

body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 12px;
    background: #e2e8f0;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #1e293b;
}

.page {
    width: 210mm;
    min-height: 297mm;
    margin: auto;
    padding: 8mm;
    background: white;
}

h1 {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    color: #1d4ed8;
    font-size: 24px;
}

.subtitle {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 11px;
    margin: 6px 0 14px;
}

.section {
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    padding: 9px;
    border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
    border-radius: 6px;
}

h2 {
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #1d4ed8;
}

p {
    margin: 4px 0 8px;
    font-size: 10px;
    line-height: 1.5;
}

.demo {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 48px;
    padding: 5px;
    gap: 5px;
    background: #eff6ff;
    border: 1px dashed #93c5fd;
}

.item {
    min-width: 35px;
    min-height: 30px;
    padding: 8px;
    background: #2563eb;
    color: white;
    text-align: center;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 10px;
}

/* JUSTIFY CONTENT */
.start { justify-content: flex-start; }
.center { justify-content: center; }
.end { justify-content: flex-end; }
.between { justify-content: space-between; }
.around { justify-content: space-around; }
.evenly { justify-content: space-evenly; }

/* ALIGN ITEMS */
.align-start { align-items: flex-start; height: 65px; }
.align-center { align-items: center; height: 65px; }
.align-end { align-items: flex-end; height: 65px; }
.stretch { align-items: stretch; height: 55px; }

.align-demo-item {
    min-height: 0;
}

/* DIRECTION */
.row { flex-direction: row; }
.column { flex-direction: column; }
.row-reverse { flex-direction: row-reverse; }

/* WRAP */
.wrap { flex-wrap: wrap; }
.nowrap { flex-wrap: nowrap; }

/* ALIGN CONTENT */
.content-center {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-content: center;
    height: 85px;
}

.content-between {
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-content: space-between;
    height: 85px;
}

/* FLEX ITEMS */
.grow-demo .grow {
    flex-grow: 1;
}

.shrink-demo .shrink {
    flex-shrink: 1;
    width: 120px;
}

.shrink-demo .no-shrink {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 120px;
}

.basis-demo .basis {
    flex-basis: 100px;
}

.self-demo {
    align-items: flex-start;
    height: 65px;
}

.self-center {
    align-self: center;
}

.self-end {
    align-self: flex-end;
}

.order-demo .first {
    order: 2;
}

.order-demo .second {
    order: 1;
}

.order-demo .third {
    order: 3;
}

.note {
    margin-top: 10px;
    padding: 8px;
    background: #fef3c7;
    font-size: 10px;
    line-height: 1.6;
}

@page {
    size: A4 portrait;
    margin: 0;
}

@media print {
    body {
        padding: 0;
        background: white;
        -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
        print-color-adjust: exact;
    }

    .page {
        width: 210mm;
        min-height: 297mm;
        margin: 0;
    }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<main class="page">

<h1>CSS FLEXBOX PROPERTIES</h1>
<div class="subtitle">
    Simple Visual Guide • Parent Properties & Item Properties
</div>

<section class="section">
<h2>1. display: flex</h2>
<p>Turns an element into a flex container. Its direct children become flex items.</p>
<div class="demo">
    <div class="item">1</div>
    <div class="item">2</div>
    <div class="item">3</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>2. flex-direction</h2>
<p>Controls the direction of the flex items.</p>
<p><b>row</b> = horizontal | <b>column</b> = vertical | <b>row-reverse</b> = reversed horizontal order</p>
<div class="demo row">
    <div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div>
</div>
<div class="demo column" style="height:115px; margin-top:5px;">
    <div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>3. justify-content</h2>
<p>Arranges items along the main axis.</p>
<p>flex-start | center | flex-end | space-between | space-around | space-evenly</p>
<div class="demo start"><div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div></div>
<div class="demo center" style="margin-top:4px;"><div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div></div>
<div class="demo between" style="margin-top:4px;"><div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div></div>
<div class="demo evenly" style="margin-top:4px;"><div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div></div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>4. align-items</h2>
<p>Aligns items along the cross axis on a single flex line.</p>
<p>flex-start | center | flex-end | stretch | baseline</p>
<div class="demo align-start"><div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div></div>
<div class="demo align-center" style="margin-top:4px;"><div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div></div>
<div class="demo align-end" style="margin-top:4px;"><div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div></div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>5. flex-wrap</h2>
<p>Controls whether items stay on one line or wrap onto new lines.</p>
<div class="demo wrap">
    <div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div>
    <div class="item">4</div><div class="item">5</div><div class="item">6</div>
    <div class="item">7</div><div class="item">8</div><div class="item">9</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>6. gap</h2>
<p>Adds space between flex items without adding space outside the container.</p>
<div class="demo" style="gap:15px;">
    <div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>7. align-content</h2>
<p>Controls spacing between multiple flex lines when wrapping occurs and extra cross-axis space is available.</p>
<div class="demo content-center">
    <div class="item">1</div><div class="item">2</div><div class="item">3</div>
    <div class="item">4</div><div class="item">5</div><div class="item">6</div>
    <div class="item">7</div><div class="item">8</div><div class="item">9</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>8. flex-grow</h2>
<p>Controls how much an item grows to use available free space.</p>
<div class="demo grow-demo">
    <div class="item">Normal</div>
    <div class="item grow">Grow 1</div>
    <div class="item grow">Grow 1</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>9. flex-shrink and flex-basis</h2>
<p><b>flex-shrink</b> controls shrinking. <b>flex-basis</b> sets an item's initial main size.</p>
<div class="demo basis-demo">
    <div class="item basis">Basis 100px</div>
    <div class="item">Normal</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>10. align-self</h2>
<p>Overrides align-items for one individual flex item.</p>
<div class="demo self-demo">
    <div class="item">Normal</div>
    <div class="item self-center">Center</div>
    <div class="item self-end">End</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<h2>11. order</h2>
<p>Changes the visual order of flex items without changing the HTML order.</p>
<div class="demo order-demo">
    <div class="item first">HTML 1 / Order 2</div>
    <div class="item second">HTML 2 / Order 1</div>
    <div class="item third">HTML 3 / Order 3</div>
</div>
</section>

<div class="note">
<b>Remember:</b> Parent properties include display, flex-direction,
flex-wrap, flex-flow, justify-content, align-items, align-content and gap.
Item properties include order, flex-grow, flex-shrink, flex-basis,
flex and align-self. The flex-flow property is a shorthand for
flex-direction and flex-wrap.
</div>

</main>
</body>
</html>
